From: 月可 <hukeyang.hky@antgroup.com>
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] KVM: retain eager PIT worker startup on Ubuntu 7.0

The 6.12 kthread_create_worker() API also starts its worker. The target
kernel separates creation from startup, following upstream b04e317b5226
("treewide: Introduce kthread_run_worker[_on_cpu]()").

Use the target run helper to preserve the baseline's eager startup. A
worker with no initial PIT work must not remain in its initialization
TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE state and produce a misleading hung-task report.
Queueing work and normal destruction can wake that state; this change
does not claim to fix a permanent PIT deadlock.

Keep this API adaptation in the target patch series so the native 6.12
baseline does not require the newer helper.

Signed-off-by: 月可 <hukeyang.hky@antgroup.com>
---
 arch/x86/kvm/i8254.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/i8254.c b/arch/x86/kvm/i8254.c
--- a/arch/x86/kvm/i8254.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/i8254.c
@@ -682,7 +682,7 @@ struct kvm_pit *kvm_create_pit(struct kvm *kvm, u32 flags)
 	pid_nr = pid_vnr(pid);
 	put_pid(pid);
 
-	pit->worker = kthread_create_worker(0, "kvm-pit/%d", pid_nr);
+	pit->worker = kthread_run_worker(0, "kvm-pit/%d", pid_nr);
 	if (IS_ERR(pit->worker))
 		goto fail_kthread;
 
